  "courseSlug": "azure-problems",
  "title": "Virtual Network Design",
  "description": "Design a secure and scalable Azure VNet with subnets, NSGs, and peering.",
  "order": 1,
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "estimatedMinutes": 20,
  "tags": ["azure", "networking", "vnet", "subnets", "nsg", "peering"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Problem Statement"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "You are designing a multi-tier application with web, app, and database tiers. You need network isolation between tiers, controlled traffic flow, and connectivity to on-premises via VPN. How do you design the VNet?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "What to Do"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Create **subnets per tier** (web, app, data). Use **NSGs** to restrict traffic (web -> app -> db only). Use **Azure Firewall** for centralized outbound control. Use **VNet Peering** or **VPN Gateway** for connectivity."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "How to Implement"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "ARM Template - VNet with Subnets and NSGs",
        "language": "json",
        "code": "{\n  \"type\": \"Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks\",\n  \"apiVersion\": \"2023-09-01\",\n  \"name\": \"vnet-prod\",\n  \"location\": \"eastus\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"addressSpace\": { \"addressPrefixes\": [\"10.0.0.0/16\"] },\n    \"subnets\": [\n      { \"name\": \"snet-web\", \"properties\": { \"addressPrefix\": \"10.0.1.0/24\" } },\n      { \"name\": \"snet-app\", \"properties\": { \"addressPrefix\": \"10.0.2.0/24\" } },\n      { \"name\": \"snet-data\", \"properties\": { \"addressPrefix\": \"10.0.3.0/24\" } }\n    ]\n  }\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "NSG Rules - Allow Web to App Only",
        "language": "json",
        "code": "{\n  \"securityRules\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Allow-Web-to-App\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"priority\": 100,\n        \"direction\": \"Inbound\",\n        \"access\": \"Allow\",\n        \"protocol\": \"Tcp\",\n        \"sourcePortRange\": \"*\",\n        \"destinationPortRange\": \"8080\",\n        \"sourceAddressPrefix\": \"10.0.1.0/24\",\n        \"destinationAddressPrefix\": \"10.0.2.0/24\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Deny-All-Inbound\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"priority\": 4096,\n        \"direction\": \"Inbound\",\n        \"access\": \"Deny\",\n        \"protocol\": \"*\",\n        \"sourcePortRange\": \"*\",\n        \"destinationPortRange\": \"*\",\n        \"sourceAddressPrefix\": \"*\",\n        \"destinationAddressPrefix\": \"*\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Why This Design"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Subnet isolation with NSGs provides **defense in depth**. Each tier can only receive traffic from the tier above it. This limits blast radius if one tier is compromised."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "comparison-cards",
      "data": {
        "title": "Network Security Comparison",
        "cards": [
          {
            "title": "NSG + Subnet Isolation",
            "description": "Standard network security",
            "pros": ["Simple to implement", "Built-in Azure feature", "No additional cost"],
            "cons": ["No application-layer inspection", "Stateful rules only"],
            "tags": ["Recommended baseline"]
          },
          {
            "title": "Azure Firewall",
            "description": "Managed firewall with FQDN filtering",
            "pros": ["Application-layer inspection", "FQDN filtering", "Threat intelligence"],
            "cons": ["Additional cost", "More complex routing"],
            "tags": ["Advanced security"]
          },
          {
            "title": "Network Virtual Appliance",
            "description": "Third-party firewall VM",
            "pros": ["Full control", "Advanced features", "Legacy compatibility"],
            "cons": ["Management overhead", "Scaling complexity"],
            "tags": ["Specialized requirements"]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
